<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chhindwara district</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Chhindwara district is a district of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madhya-pradesh">Madhya Pradesh</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, on the Satpura plateau, with its headquarters at the town of Chhindwara. It has a large Gond population and was the heartland of the Gond kingdom of Deogarh, whose rulers founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nagpur">Nagpur</a>. Part of the Pench National Park lies within it.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/chhindwara-district.jpg" alt="Chhindwara district" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Kmohankar · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Badal_Mahal,_Deogarh_Fort.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
